# CKA Lab Exercise: Custom Resource Definitions (CRDs) & Operator Concepts

Hands-on training scenario for the Certified Kubernetes Administrator (CKA) certification, covering CustomResourceDefinition (CRD) schema specification, OpenAPI v3 structural validation, additional printer columns, and custom resource lifecycle.

---

## 1. Overview & Objectives

Operators and custom controllers rely on CRDs to extend the core Kubernetes API:

- **Section 1: CustomResourceDefinition (CRD)**: Authoring `apiextensions.k8s.io/v1` definitions with custom group, version, kind, plural, singular, and short names.
- **Section 2: OpenAPI v3 Structural Validation**: Enforcing schema validation (`required` fields, minimum/maximum values, enums) at admission time.
- **Section 3: Custom Resource Lifecycle**: Instantiating custom objects, verifying CLI additional columns, and validating admission rejection on malformed specs.

